00:10:28.027 --> 00:10:28.894
in this race, who I think

00:10:28.894 --> 00:10:29.595
would have been

00:10:29.595 --> 00:10:30.196
a far

00:10:30.196 --> 00:10:30.663
stronger

00:10:30.663 --> 00:10:31.430
candidate in this race.

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:32.164
And we're probably up there

00:10:32.164 --> 00:10:33.499
giving a speech tonight

00:10:33.499 --> 00:10:34.634
instead of John Fetterman.

00:10:34.634 --> 00:10:35.234
And so

00:10:35.234 --> 00:10:35.701
a lot of people

00:10:35.701 --> 00:10:36.068
are going to ask

00:10:36.068 --> 00:10:37.136
questions about

00:10:37.136 --> 00:10:39.438
how can you lay this loss

00:10:39.438 --> 00:10:40.439
at the feet of the president

00:10:40.439 --> 00:10:41.207
the former president?

00:10:41.207 --> 00:10:42.241
People are going to ask that

00:10:42.241 --> 00:10:43.142
come in tomorrow

00:10:43.142 --> 00:10:44.043
and the day after the day

00:10:44.043 --> 00:10:44.877
after Pennsylvania.

00:10:44.877 --> 00:10:45.945
And what Governor

00:10:45.945 --> 00:10:46.846
I said, Governor,

00:10:46.846 --> 00:10:48.280
you lost a governor's mansion

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:49.215
and a Senate race

00:10:49.215 --> 00:10:50.549
in Pennsylvania tonight.

00:10:50.549 --> 00:10:52.318
And and I know Republicans

00:10:52.318 --> 00:10:54.020
across the commonwealth are

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:54.854
pretty upset right now.

